g":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.5-beta2 and 4.5-beta3\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta3 - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA RTX A1000 Laptop GPU - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-12800H (20 threads) - 31.67 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using a screen reader to navigate the menu bar containing options like new scene, new inherited scene, open scene, etc., some options get skipped, e.g.:\n- Go into menu, hear: \"New Scene   1 of 23\"\n- Hit down arrow, hear: \"New Inherited Scene...   2 of 23\"\n- Hit down arrow, hear: \"Open Scene...   3 of 23\"\n- Hit down arrow, hear: \"Open Recent   5 of 23\"\n\nThis is present in all tabs, not just the one dealing with scenes/scripts.\n\nIn addition, sometimes pressing down or up arrow skips to a seemingly random option within the menus. This is often after one switches menus, e.g., from the menu containing options for things like project settings back to one containing the new scene option. Pressing down arrow at this point often snaps one to 8th, 12th, 17th option with no rhyme or reason behind it. This behavior is inconsistent.\n\nIncidentally, this bug (skipping menu options) also impacts usage of the inspector. It's particularly impactful when selecting things like value types for a dictionary (some options just downright get skipped when using up/down arrow keys).\n\n\nExpected behavior: one should be able to arrow up/down inside the menus and not have the sporadic option skips.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create any project inside Godot.\n- Go to the menu bar containing the options for things like creating new scene\n- Use up/down arrows with screen reader\n- Witness the bug.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/user